==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|heben}}, {{m|gmh|heven}} (rarer {{m|gmh|heffen}}), from {{inh|de|goh|heffen}}, {{m|goh|heven}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*habbjan}}. Compare {{cog|nl|heffen}}, {{cog|en|heave}}, {{cog|da|hæve}}. {{doublet|de|hieven|kapieren}}.

The ''-b-'' is regular in the past tense and participle. In Middle High German the paradigm was regularised by spreading ''-b-'' to the present tense; reinforced in [[East Central German]] by the local shift ''-v-'' → ''-b-'' (as in {{m|gmw-ecg|Oben}} for {{m|de|Ofen}}). The fricative is preserved in related {{m|de|Hefe|t=yeast}}. The original past forms {{m|de|hub}}, {{m|de|gehaben}} were retained until Early Modern German. The verb was then shifted to the class of {{m|de|fliegen}} etc. (Compare {{m+|nl|heffen}}, which was also shifted, though to a different ablaut class.)

